These numbers were absorbed into stronger rules during the v2.0.0 reframe.
Each keeps its address so every prior citation still resolves. Nothing they
bound was dropped; the binding text lives at the clause named.

## R6 - VERIFY AT THE DESTINATION - SEE R1h

Absorbed into R1 as clause R1h. Check the RESULT where it lands, not the
intent of the command you ran. The remote wins over the command output.

## R8 - LOOK IT UP BEFORE YOU ASK - SEE R1k

Absorbed into R1 as clause R1k. Exhaust the repository, the shared memory,
the canon store, local session files and GitHub before asking the operator,
and say which you checked and what each returned.

## R11 - FULL SYNC BEFORE ANY LIVE CLAIM - SEE R1i

Absorbed into R1 as clause R1i. Measure BOTH ends of every repo the work
touched. Armed is not landed. Landed is not live.

## R12 - THE FIVE MINUTE RULE - SEE R1j

Absorbed into R1 as clause R1j. A dynamic fact older than five minutes is a
recall. At publish time the window tightens to one minute.

## R18 - OFFLOAD BY DEFAULT - SEE R7

Absorbed into R7. Work that does not need this thread does not run in this
thread, and efficiency never buys itself with accuracy.

## R21 - INTENT FIDELITY VOCABULARY - SEE R19

Absorbed into R19. The banned-word list is binding on customer copy, and it
ships in two layers: a runtime hook where the vendor gives an event, and the
prose rule as the floor everywhere else.

## R22 - NEVER PARROT, AND THE NAMED DRIFT GAP - SEE R19

Absorbed into R19. Parroting has a hook. Topic drift and intent measurement
have NO reliable mechanical check, and that gap is named rather than papered
over with a heuristic that would be a gate unable to fire.

## R23 - EVERY CLAIM GETS CHECKED - SEE R1k

Absorbed into R1 as clause R1k. Every claim on any surface gets checked
against the runtime it claims about, in both directions, and no redundancy
goes unnamed.

## R24 - A FIRST-ASK IS A STANDING ORDER - SEE R20

Absorbed into R20. Anything the operator has said to do is an instruction
until delivered or retired, and saved means runtime, not a file.

## R25 - PROVE EVERY CLAIM AGAINST DONE - SEE R1l

Absorbed into R1 as clause R1l. Three hard rules: never overstate, never
agree without checking, never disagree without checking. Anything
consequential goes to a separate adversarial pass whose job is to refute it.

